<%# locals: (workspace:) -%>
<%# The identity-bar workspace name — links to the Overview. Rendered from
    both shared/_workspace_identity_bar and workspaces/update.turbo_stream so
    the live bar and the Turbo broadcast target can never drift apart.

    items-start + leading-tight are load-bearing, not taste: together they put
    the text's top edge on the identity-bar logo's (measured — items-center sat
    11px low, default leading 3px low, leading-none 2px high).

    min-h-[44px] is not optional: spec/support/axe_accessibility.rb's
    mc-target-size-44 check measures this element's own box and grants no
    Equivalent exception, so dropping it fails ~98 system specs even though
    the sidebar's Overview item reaches the same destination at 44px. It costs
    22px of dead space under the name, which is why the role line below cannot
    sit inside a 40px logo's height. -%>
<%= link_to workspace_path(workspace),
      id: "workspace-name-heading",
      aria: { label: t("workspaces.identity_bar.overview_link_label", name: workspace.name) },
      class: "min-h-[44px] min-w-11 inline-flex items-start text-lg leading-tight font-bold text-text-heading truncate rounded focus-ring hover:text-interactive" do %>
  <%= workspace.name %>
<% end %>
